Refactored the repo from a single mixed-purpose source file into a reusable heap implementation in [MinHeap.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/011_binary_heap/MinHeap.java:3) and a small executable test harness in [MinHeapTest.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/011_binary_heap/MinHeapTest.java:1). The heap logic is cleaner now: sift-up/sift-down are isolated helpers, naming is normalized, size/state helpers were added, and invalid index / empty-heap cases now fail explicitly instead of relying on accidental array behavior.

The main quality changes are in [MinHeap.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/011_binary_heap/MinHeap.java:7), [MinHeap.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/011_binary_heap/MinHeap.java:86), and [MinHeap.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/011_binary_heap/MinHeap.java:127): constructor validation, iterative heap maintenance, and explicit bounds/empty checks. I also replaced the old print-only demo with repeatable checks in [MinHeapTest.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/011_binary_heap/MinHeapTest.java:10) covering the original example flow, full-capacity behavior, value changes in both directions, and invalid-index handling.

